{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Reframe / outpaint video (Wan2.2 Fun VACE)",
    "description": "Core nodes only. The source clip is trimmed from the start to the window, resampled to 16 fps, fitted inside the target canvas (9:16 480x832, 16:9 832x480, 1:1 624x624, 4:5 512x640) and padded with ImagePadForOutpaint; the pad mask (repeated per frame) tells WanVaceToVideo which pixels to generate, the original pixels are kept as control. Two-stage Wan2.2 sampling (8 steps, shift 8): high-noise model without LoRA at cfg 3.5 for steps 0-4 (prompt adherence), low-noise model + lightx2v 4-step LoRA at cfg 1 for steps 4-8. speed=fast puts the high-noise LoRA (node 5) in and runs 4 steps at cfg 1 on both stages. Length 4n+1 frames (<= 81, 5 s). Source audio is not carried over."
  },
  "1": {
    "class_type": "UNETLoader",
    "inputs": {
      "unet_name": "wan2.2_fun_vace_high_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors",
